# Contributing to netbox-unifi-sync

This project is designed to be easy to work on without requiring the maintainer to hand-hold every step.

## Quick start

1. Fork and clone the repo.
2. Create a Python virtual environment.
3. Install dependencies and the package in editable mode.
4. Run lint and tests.
5. Open a focused PR.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-user>/netbox-unifi-sync.git
cd netbox-unifi-sync
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r requirements.txt
pip install -e .
ruff check netbox_unifi_sync/
pytest -q
```

## Local NetBox validation

For end-to-end validation, see `deploy/netbox-docker/README.md`.

## Contribution standards

- Keep changes small and reviewable.
- Prefer one issue -> one PR.
- Add or update tests for behavior changes.
- Document user-visible changes.
- Avoid committing secrets or local environment details.

## Before opening a PR

- Confirm the change is needed and documented.
- Run the relevant lint/test commands.
- Include a short summary of the problem and the fix.

## Maintainer policy

This repository is maintained in spare time. Contributions are welcome, and the project is organized so contributors can independently validate and submit work without a long setup process.
